WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.990
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.460
Mr. Grizzly Goes on an Adventure.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.120
It's the season when polar 
bears are delicious.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:44.580
You mean to tell me

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:48.040
that you've eaten a polar bear before?

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:51.320
Yes, I even had one this afternoon.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.000
During the summer, polar bears...

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.420
are especially delicious.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.010
An otter ate Polar Bear?!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.250
Impossible! You did it yourself?!

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.890
Oh no, there was a whole group of us.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.400
A group of you ate Polar Bear?

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.170
How dare someone who eats bears eat here!

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:24.240
It can't be!

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:29.500
Polar Bear would never be 
eaten by the likes of them!

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:32.210
This Afternoon

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.150
This afternoon.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:39.460
Try Our New Polar Bear

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:39.460
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.360
"Try Our New Polar Bear"?

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.070
Welcome.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:47.520
I'm sorry, Polar Bear.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.020
About what, Panda?

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:56.140
All this time I thought that 
you were a polar bear,

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:58.790
but I guess you weren't 
a polar bear yet.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.490
What are you talking about, Panda?

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:06.240
The sign out front said, 
"Try Our New Polar Bear."

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:08.260
No, that says...

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:10.860
So were you just white up until now?

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.670
Or just a bear?

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.890
No, "Polar Bear"

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:16.630
is the name of the a shaved ice dessert.

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:18.930
So it's shaved ice?

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:22.590
Yes. It has condensed milk and fruits on it.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:25.160
The name came from how 
the fruits are arranged.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:27.970
It looks like a polar bear's face.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:30.790
I don't need your boring 
explanation, Mr. Penguin,

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.560
I just want to eat it.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.200
How about listening to 
the whole explanation

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.630
before determining that it's boring.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.570
This is the Polar Bear.

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:41.720
Look at it from above.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:45.490
It's true!

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.120
It's a polar bear!

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:51.370
Eating a Polar Bear at 
Polar Bear's Café?

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:54.320
My, how cool.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.610
Yeah, really cool...

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:01.280
And Currently

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:00.910
And currently...

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:04.010
Say it ain't so, Polar Bear!

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:16.670
See? It was a complete lie.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:34.870
<i>It can't be! It's true?!</i>

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:38.840
Thank you for the meal!

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.710
I-It can't be!

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:47.780
Try Our New Polar Bear.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:47.780
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:47.760
"Try Our New Polar Bear."

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:51.220
Whaddya mean you've begun?!

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.480
That means your life has ended!

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:59.840
I don't think the

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.520
habaneros are a good idea.

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:02.910
They're entirely too hot!

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:03.650
Really?

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:07.580
Habaneros get addicting after a while.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:14.660
Here I go!

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:15.950
Over here!

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:16.720
Polar Bear...

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:16.820
Go!

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:20.630
We've been hanging out 
since we were kids.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:24.590
I wanna eat honey!

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:27.540
You sure that's a good 
idea, Polar Bear?

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.980
You can do it!

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:42.230
I wanna eat some smelts!

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:44.110
You sure that's a good 
idea, Polar Bear?

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:50.130
I wanna eat mushrooms!

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:51.870
You sure that's a good 
idea, Polar Bear?!

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:57.060
Hey, wait!

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.060
I don't...

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.820
seem to have too many good memories.

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:02.790
But they're nostalgic.

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:08.000
This ain't good. 
I keep thinking about you.

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:13.180
Polar Bear!

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.060
Welcome.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:29.090
Polar Bear!

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:46.870
Polar Bear!

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:52.620
Wanna buy a beer <i>(bi-ru)</i>?

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:53.860
Already brought one.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:55.340
See?

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.600
That would be a reel <i>(ri-ru)</i>.

00:06:58.540 --> 00:06:59.700
Puns?!

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:06.960
P-P-Polar Bear!

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.440
Oh, solitude...

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:11.830
help to sooth my sadness!

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:14.970
It's a bear! How cute!

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:16.250
What are you doing?

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:17.690
Look over here!

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.500
Hey, is it true that Mr. Grizzly's place

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.110
has been closed for a while?

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.870
He could be on a trip somewhere.

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:30.470
A trip, huh?

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:34.260
I bet it's a really wild trip.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:37.100
Probably.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:42.760
Grizzly heads aimlessly to the north.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:48.960
He stops by a small bar.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:50.920
There you go.

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.040
I didn't order that.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.310
It's on the house.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:57.580
You're traveling, aren't you?

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:00.540
Can you tell?

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:04.010
You smell of the city.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:08.710
And then a bad-looking man appears.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:11.760
Hey there, Foxy, I decided 
to stop by again.

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:13.320
Go on home!

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:14.760
Because of you, all my

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.890
other customers won't come here anymore!

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:19.890
Better watch your tone or else...

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.620
Leave.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:25.360
If you have a problem, 
you'll have to deal with me.

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:26.560
Sorry!

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:29.590
Thank you so much.

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:32.000
Thanks for the salmon.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:38.200
And so, Grizzly became the 
bar's bouncer.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:38.200
Sake

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:38.200
Red Fox's Bar

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:38.200
Beware of Bear

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:41.380
The Fox's young children also 
took a liking to Grizzly.

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:43.710
Uncle Grizzly!

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.570
He also got along with the 
elderly in the area.

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:48.260
Sorry for the trouble.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:49.670
Not a problem!

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:55.250
Before they knew it, life was 
unimaginable without Grizzly.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:58.490
Really?

00:08:58.890 --> 00:08:59.970
Panda,

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:03.640
you can't take stories with 
no sense of reality seriously.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.800
Who knew things would come to this.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:10.960
How bout a cup, Mr. Griz?

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:14.550
How 'bout some salmon <i>(shake)</i> 
to go with that sake?

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:19.160
Polar... Bear...

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:22.000
I told you, no puns!

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.600
Sorry...

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:29.970
<i>In the end, we live in 
a dog-eat-dog world.</i>

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:34.330
<i>I'm not gonna cry anymore!</i>

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:37.620
Bye!

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:37.620
Come back anytime!

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:38.790
Bye-bye!

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:40.450
Take of yourself!

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:44.750
So long, Polar Bear!

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:51.320
Try Our New Polar Bear

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:51.320
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:56.280
I'm going to take over this café!

00:09:57.920 --> 00:09:59.830
What brought this on all of a sudden?

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:02.300
The only one that can take his place

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:04.280
is me, his best friend.

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:06.500
I'll be the polar bear!

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:09.460
So you're gonna be the owner 
of Polar Bear Café?

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:11.970
Starting today, call me the manager.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:14.150
What about Grizzly's Bar?

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:15.190
I'll do it!

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:16.840
I'll work day and night!

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:18.870
When will you sleep?

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:20.690
In between.

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:23.490
I'll even make puns!

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:26.000
Since that's what makes this place...

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:33.250
That would be sister <i>(sisuta)</i>!

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:35.330
Then...

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:45.530
That would be Easter <i>(I-suta)</i>!

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:47.880
Then how about this?!

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:52.080
That would be a poster <i>(posuta)</i>!

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:54.710
This would be a duster <i>(dasuta)</i>.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.960
Don't wipe my face with a duster!

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:04.180
Why the hell are you alive?!

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:06.810
Because my mom gave birth to me.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:08.110
That's not what I meant!

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:10.140
I thought the otters ate you!

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:12.530
Hey!

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.150
Came by to eat the Polar Bear again.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:16.700
Huh?

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:20.580
What the hell is going on?!

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:28.080
Y-You shouldn't have given 
it such a misleading name!

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:31.020
Damn it, you scared me.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:34.170
How are you going to repay 
the time I spent in sadne—

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:42.510
Was it such a shock that it brings you 
to tears just thinking about it?

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:46.260
I've got brain freeze!

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:52.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:51.660
A Strange Restaurant.

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:58.120
<i>It was on a hot summer day,</i>

00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:00.520
<i>when my work first brought me to that town.</i>

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:04.530
<i>The thing that irritated me most</i>

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:07.460
<i>in the undying heat and humidity</i>

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:11.010
<i>was the Chinese restaurant by the 
station I went to for lunch.</i>

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:15.600
<i>The humid interior.</i>

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:18.300
<i>The cold noodles weren't cold,</i>

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:20.530
<i>and had been sitting too long.</i>

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:25.020
<i>But my pride doesn't allow me</i>

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:26.930
<i>not to finish something I had ordered.</i>

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:28.470
<i>But...</i>

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:31.330
<i>My stomach was still heavy.</i>

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.450
<i>I must refresh myself.</i>

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:45.010
<i>There are a lot of risks</i>

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:47.230
<i>in going into an unknown café</i>

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:49.150
<i>in an unknown town.</i>

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:55.780
<i>I feel alive again!</i>

00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:56.990
Welcome!

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.760
Please sit anywhere you'd like.

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:05.370
That's...

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:07.830
Oh, that's Mr. Polar Bear.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.680
Yes, I can see that.

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:11.520
He's the owner.

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:16.120
A polar bear is the owner?

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:18.830
Indeed. It is Polar 
Bear's Café, after all.

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:21.650
I-I see...

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:24.030
Today's Pasta 
Today's Lunch Plate 
Omelet Rice 
Chicken and Veggie Hot Sandwich 
Onion Soup w/ Lettuce Fried Rice 
Special

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:24.030
Bamboo (Large Serving Available) 
Bamboo Grass 
(Large Serving Available)

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:24.030
Coffee (Hot or Iced) / Black Tea (Hot or Iced) 
Houji Tea / Jasmine Tea / Corn Tea 
 Orange Juice / Grapefruit Juice / Ginger Ale

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:24.030
Welcome.

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:26.890
I'll be happy to take your 
order whenever you're ready.

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:28.480
T-Thank you.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:35.000
<i>I don't see a zipper.</i>

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:38.210
<i>Apparently, it's not a costume, 
but rather the real deal.</i>

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:42.380
<i>I heard that there were a lot 
of animals in this town,</i>

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:45.240
<i>but this is the first time 
I've seen a working animal.</i>

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:48.680
<i>It's huge...</i>

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:51.360
<i>Does he cook with those huge hands?</i>

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:01.460
<i>Cutting fish into round 
slices at a café?</i>

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:02.650
<i>Inconceivable!</i>

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:05.260
<i>But that's all I can think of.</i>

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:14.650
<i>Such flawless and elegant movement!</i>

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:17.690
<i>I take back any doubts.</i>

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:20.840
<i>Now, I'm going to throw away 
any prejudices and order.</i>

00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:23.920
<i>What if the menu's only for animals?!</i>

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:27.720
<i>Oh, it's rather normal.</i>

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:29.900
<i>This is...</i>

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.300
<i>Bamboo?!</i>

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:35.360
<i>Wait a minute,</i>

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:38.580
<i>it could just mean some dessert 
made to look like bamboo.</i>

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:42.710
<i>But I can't rule out the possibility 
that it's actually bamboo...</i>

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:46.680
Are you ready to order?

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:50.180
U-Uh... Iced coffee.

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:52.760
Does one iced coffee 
complete your order?

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.320
Yes...

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:55.790
No!

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:00.830
Bamboo.

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:03.790
Did you say bamboo?

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:06.250
Yes.

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:09.240
We have a larger serving, if you'd like.

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:10.070
What?!

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.790
I'll uh, take that, then.

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:13.690
Yes, sir.

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:17.690
<i>I ended up ordering it.</i>

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:19.370
<i>And I made it a larger serving!</i>

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:25.690
<i>Will this decision turn 
out good or bad?</i>

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:27.650
Here you go.

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:31.330
<i>It was bad!</i>

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:32.580
<i>Wait a sec.</i>

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.970
<i>Maybe it's just no one's ever 
tried to eat it before</i>

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:36.520
<i>and it's actually pretty good.</i>

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:39.100
<i>Yeah, that's gotta be it!</i>

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:48.260
<i>The bamboo aroma is 
slowly turning bitter</i>

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:49.990
<i>and filling my mouth, along with the</i>

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:52.010
<i>fibers that I can't chew through.</i>

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:56.670
<i>It's just ordinary bamboo.</i>

00:15:58.550 --> 00:16:00.060
<i>What am I going to do?</i>

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.530
<i>Should I just quietly spit it out?</i>

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:05.150
<i>But it's unthinkable to spit out</i>

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.020
<i>something I've already put in my mouth.</i>

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:09.710
<i>But even if I try to 
will myself to eat it,</i>

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:11.330
<i>my body is resisting!</i>

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:13.090
<i>Water! I need water!</i>

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:15.920
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:19.030
<i>I drank it all earlier!</i>

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:21.870
<i>I've reached my limit!</i>

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:23.830
Here's your iced coffee.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.700
<i>Saved from above!</i>

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.780
<i>The battle has only begun...</i>

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:47.240
Hello!

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:48.190
<i>A panda!</i>

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:49.650
There we go.

00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:53.570
<i>It's a panda.</i>

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:59.030
Giant 
Panda (from China)

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:58.730
<i>I saw just the head of a panda once,
 when I went to the zoo as a kid...</i>

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:02.020
<i>and now one is sitting right next to me!</i>

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:07.560
<i>But he's sitting so close that 
it'd be awkward to look!</i>

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:09.080
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:12.320
<i>I know!</i>

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:14.030
<i>I'll pretend I'm looking around.</i>

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:18.930
U-Um, I wonder where the bathroom is...

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:24.070
<i>He's staring at me!</i>

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:27.350
<i>The panda is totally staring at me!</i>

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:30.360
Aren't you going to eat that?

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:31.090
Huh?

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:34.480
I'll take it off your 
hands if you want.

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:39.280
<i>I can't let this chance slip by.</i>

00:17:39.590 --> 00:17:41.680
H-Here, help yourself.

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:43.100
Wow, thank you!

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:45.630
<i>Crisis adverted!</i>

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:47.840
I apologize.

00:17:48.350 --> 00:17:50.250
<i>Oh, no problem at all.</i>

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:53.210
Here, you can have another.

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:55.170
It's on the house.

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:02.260
<i>I'm right back where I started.</i>

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:05.100
Welcome.

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:06.980
Hey.

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:09.060
<i>Now a penguin?!</i>

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:11.260
<i>It's so cute.</i>

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.990
<i>Does it plan to sit on that stool?!</i>

00:18:16.690 --> 00:18:18.860
<i>Is he going to climb up? Fly up?</i>

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:20.610
<i>Is someone going to lift him up?</i>

00:18:21.650 --> 00:18:23.820
Would you like a refill on your coffee?

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:26.550
Th-Thank you very much.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:33.110
<i>Damn it! I missed it!</i>

00:18:33.110 --> 00:18:34.880
It's pretty hot today.

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:36.400
I know.

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:38.840
I want an air conditioner 
<i>(ku-ra)</i> at work, too.

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:42.600
Those would be curlers <i>(ka-ra)</i>.

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:45.780
That would be sailor 
<i>(se-ra)</i> style uniform.

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:48.840
That would be a dealer <i>(di-ra)</i>.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:51.730
That's...

00:18:54.470 --> 00:18:55.730
What is it, again?

00:18:56.430 --> 00:18:58.380
Something "ra"?

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:00.690
Ra, ra...

00:19:01.270 --> 00:19:02.240
Ma-ra?

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:03.730
Trailer <i>(Tore-ra)</i>?

00:19:05.070 --> 00:19:06.460
<i>It's hustler </i>(hasura)<i>!</i>

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:08.600
<i>Hustler!</i>

00:19:09.550 --> 00:19:10.730
I can't remember.

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:13.170
Tell us!

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:16.130
It's... a... secret.

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:18.750
<i>I want to say it!</i>

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:20.940
<i>I really want to say it!</i>

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:23.850
<i>But I can't just butt into 
the conversation...</i>

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:26.580
Oh, I know, a wrestler <i>(resura)</i>!

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:28.600
<i>So close!</i>

00:19:29.190 --> 00:19:31.070
Then, broiler <i>(buroira)</i>!

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:33.560
<i>So far!</i>

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:35.780
<i>I can't hold it any longer!</i>

00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:38.330
<i>I'll say it, no matter what
 they may think of me!</i>

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:39.740
Hu—

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:41.290
Welcome.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:47.700
<i>Another idol from the zoo, the koala!</i>

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:50.710
<i>The ever-popular otter!</i>

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:53.470
<i>The colorful mandrill!</i>

00:19:58.130 --> 00:19:59.630
<i>A camel?</i>

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:02.880
<i>A donkey? No...</i>

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:06.170
<i>A tama? No, but it's 
something like that...</i>

00:20:07.090 --> 00:20:10.420
<i>I can't remember! Damn it!</i>

00:20:11.300 --> 00:20:13.110
Welcome, Mr. Llama.

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:15.020
<i>That's it! It's a llama!</i>

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:20.120
<i>I feel so much better!</i>

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:29.240
Mr. Handa was really funny the other day.

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:31.990
He was, it was rather impressive.

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:34.240
<i>Suddenly, I'm completely 
surrounded by animals...</i>

00:20:31.990 --> 00:20:34.440
Mr. Penguin was impressive himself.

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:37.170
Who knew Mr. Handa had 
that side to him?

00:20:34.650 --> 00:20:36.710
<i>Not to mention they all 
seem to be regulars...</i>

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:38.620
I know!

00:20:38.810 --> 00:20:40.580
<i>I feel awkward being here.</i>

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:40.170
Indeed.

00:20:44.650 --> 00:20:46.970
A-All the seats are full!

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:49.100
There're some tables open, though.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.410
U-Um...

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:51.730
You can have my seat.

00:20:51.730 --> 00:20:53.400
I'm about to head out, so...

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:56.840
What? You're already going home?

00:20:56.840 --> 00:20:59.070
You should stay a while longer.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:01.300
When did you two get so close?

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:04.780
Mr. Necktie gave me his bamboo.

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:07.240
Right?

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:12.080
Yes.

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:16.270
Thank you very much.

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:18.290
Thank you.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:19.820
Pardon me.

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:21.130
Yes?

00:21:21.560 --> 00:21:24.310
You can get it to go, so here you go.

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:27.990
Thank you very much.

00:21:32.510 --> 00:21:33.350
Now, then...

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:37.930
Guess I'll get back to work.

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:46.280
<i>And so I worked until the sun set,</i>

00:21:48.310 --> 00:21:50.780
<i>and welcomed night in this town.</i>

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:56.160
Maybe I'll get a drink.

00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:05.800
That spot there's open.

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:06.900
Have a seat.

00:22:08.080 --> 00:22:10.010
Um, I...

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:12.940
Sit down. There's no need to hold back.

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:17.130
<i>There are a lot of risks</i>

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:21.300
<i>in going into an unknown shop...</i>

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:26.270
Next Time

00:23:58.040 --> 00:23:59.530
Hey, Panda, Panda.

00:23:59.530 --> 00:24:00.960
What is it, Mr. Penguin?

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:02.630
I'm always on the receiving end,

00:24:02.630 --> 00:24:04.310
so I thought I'd strike first.

00:24:04.310 --> 00:24:05.470
So, Panda—

00:24:05.470 --> 00:24:09.610
More importantly, look at 
what Mr. Llama has become.

00:24:09.610 --> 00:24:13.260
Does listening to me not 
exist in your dictionary?

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:14.680
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:14.680 --> 00:24:16.300
Next time on Polar Bear's Café,

00:24:16.880 --> 00:24:19.050
we'll be presenting, 
"Goodbye, Mr. Penguin."

00:24:19.050 --> 00:24:20.600
Wait, I'm still here! 
I'll always be here!

00:24:20.600 --> 00:24:21.260
Goodbye.

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:22.830
Let's Go Camping!
Rin Rin and the High School Girl

00:24:21.260 --> 00:24:22.830
I'm here! I'm still here!
